    "raw": "Phase changes: 317.3 K, melting point of P; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 0.157$ kcal/mol. \n550 K, boiling point of P to $P_{4}(g)$ ; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 2.908$ kcal/mol of P. \n561 K, melting point of $P_{4}S10$ ; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 9.820$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td>298.15-561 K:</td><td> $Cp^o$  = 58.974 + 51.176 $x10^{-3}T$  - 3.105 $x10^5T^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td>561-787 K:</td><td> $H^o-H_2^o_{98}$  = 58.974 $x10^{-3}T$  + 25.588 $x10^{-6}T^2$  + 3.105 $x10^2T^{-1}$  - 20.899 $Cp^o$  = 141.457 $H^o-H_2^o_{98}$  = 141.457 $x10^{-3}T$  - 48.745</td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-317.3 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -245.761 + 2.063x10^{-3}T + 11.248x10^{-6}T^{2} - 31.000T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -245.761 - 2.063x10^{-3}T\\ln T - 11.248x10^{-6}T^{2} - 15.500T^{-1} + 240.920x10^{-3}T$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">317.3-550 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -244.508 - 7.909x10^{-3}T + 23.988x10^{-6}T^{2} - 31.000T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -244.508 + 7.909x10^{-3}T\\ln T - 23.988x10^{-6}T^{2} - 15.500T^{-1} + 183.575x10^{-3}T$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">550-561 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -258.349 - 2.557x10^{-3}T + 23.972x10^{-6}T^{2} - 432.200T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -258.349 + 2.557x10^{-3}T\\ln T - 23.972x10^{-6}T^{2} - 216.100T^{-1} + 243.166x10^{-3}T$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">561-787 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -286.195 + 79.926x10^{-3}T - 1.616x10^{-6}T^{2} - 742.700T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -286.195 - 79.926x10^{-3}T\\ln T + 1.616x10^{-6}T^{2} - 371.350T^{-1} + 801.036x10^{-3}T$ </td></tr></table>\nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K based on Vincent (124) and Cueilleron (27) and P(white). Low-temperature heat capacities and entropy at 298 K from Clever (21). High-temperature data based on Peters (98). "